A||N||7||MickeyAsh||'86 V6 GT dies at 3500 RPM||||11||
Z||000000||MickeyAsh||09-11-2000||03:25 AM||||Recently my GT died on me at a red light, after stumbling and choking as I braked, I replaced the ignition module, which got it to crank again. I proceeded to drive it around, and when I floored it, the engine got to 3500 RPM, died, and then came back with a HUGE backfire after coasting for a while. I reproduced the occurence 3 times, each time with a backfire. I then replaced the ignition coil, pickup coil, rotor, distributor cap, and plug wires, but it still dies at 3500 RPM. If I'm driving it, it backfires, and then comes back and is drivable, if it's in neutral or park, it dies at 3500, and completely shuts off.<BR>(By the way: I'm getting code 42 from the ALDL)||||reg||11
Z||000001||Jim's87GT||09-11-2000||09:31 AM||||I think you'll want to check the Catalytic Converter.  The symptoms sound like a clogged cat.  They can be tough to loosen if the clamps are rusted shut but it's a good bet that the performance problems you're haveing can be cured by putting on a new converter.  A lot of folks think it should be removed and not fixed but it's easier to just get a new high flow unit and enjoy your ride.  Good luck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||MickeyAsh||09-11-2000||01:38 PM||||Hmmm.... a few questions:<BR>1) How sure are you that it's not the computer<BR>2) Is there any way to check my current cat to make sure that's the problem<BR>3) How much will a cat cost me<BR>4) Where can I get one<BR>5) Can I install it myself<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000003||Wade87GT||09-11-2000||02:13 PM||||Mine was doing the same thing just recently. I did all the things you did before I had to turn it over to a shop. They claimed it was a bad fuel pump (20 psi instead of 45-47). I'd check for a clogged fuel filter or bad gas first, which I should have done myself. When my cat clogged up a few years ago, the car almost instantly overheated above 2500 RPMs. With no place for that amount of exhaust gasses to go, it boiled the coolant flowing through the heads. With that in mind, if your cat is even somewhat clogged, I would think you should have an elevated temp reading. Especially at higher RPMs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wade87GT||09-11-2000||02:20 PM||||Another thing, even if you don't need a new cat. Take Jim's advice and put on a high flow aftermarket one. The originals were designed to last about five years, anything after that is a bonus. You'll love the results. I paid $120. for the whole job ($75. for the cat). ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Jim's87GT||09-12-2000||08:49 AM||||One way to check the cat without removing it is to take off the EGR valve.  It's no picnic but it's a LOT easier that getting the exhaust fittings off just to "check".  Be careful however, when you take the EGR off it will do a couple of things, one of which is to create a HUGE vacuum leak that runs your idle up to around 4,000 RPM.  In my case that was a frightening but welcome sign since it got to where the engine wouldn't rev over about 2,800 RPM with the clogged cat in line.  Give it a shot.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000006||fierocrazy||09-12-2000||11:08 AM||||this may sound funny but how is the idle ?  My buddy had the same problem, he replaced his Idle Control Vavle...  worked for him anyway||||reg||1
Z||000007||MickeyAsh||09-12-2000||02:05 PM||||The idle was HORRIBLE until I replaced the pickup coil... but now it stays pretty level. Sometimes it jumps around a bit, I haven't really observed it enough to give any specifics... it'd sure be nice if it were the cat, but it really seems like something electrical. Yesterday I also noticed a problem with downshifting, I attempted to floor it to down shift, and I had the pedal to the floor, yet it stayed in third (I think) until about 2200 rpm, when it finally kicked into second, and raced under the light... I tried flooring it again numerous times after that to no avail... same problem each time. And again, I don't think the cat would fire off code 42... if anyone can think of a reason it would, please tell me...||||reg||1
